\section{Introduction}\label{sec:introduction}
In this paper, we consider the following nonlinear fractional diffusion equation
\begin{equation}\label{eq:fracdiff}
    \partial_t u(x,t) = -(-\Delta)^{\alpha/2}u(x,t) + f(u(x,t)),\quad (x,t)\in D\times(0,T],
where $D=(0,1)$, $T>0$ and $0<\alpha<2$. Here $(-\Delta)^{\alpha/2}$ denotes the fractional Laplacian operator with $0<\alpha<2$, which is defined as follows:
