We perform Monte Carlo simulations using the Hybrid Monte Carlo algorithm. We use the stout smearing technique to improve the signal-to-noise ratio. We perform simulations at several values of the inverse gauge coupling $\beta$. We use the following values of $\beta$: $\beta = 7.5$, $\beta = 8.0$, and $\beta = 8.5$. These correspond to temperatures of $T = 1.2 T_c$, $T = 1.4 T_c$, and $T = 1.6 T_c$, respectively. We also perform simulations at several values of the baryon chemical potential. We use the following values of the baryon chemical potential: $\mu_B = 0$, $\mu_B = 1.5 T_c$, and $\mu_B = 2.0 T_c$. 

